  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "La pizarra de turnos",
    "overview": "The app is the office shift whiteboard. White enamel sits inside a blue-grey aluminum frame. Four markers write on it: blue for action and navigation, red for urgency and column headers, green for done, and ink black for everything else. People are round or pill-shaped color magnets with a short, real drop shadow. Activities move across columns (Pendiente, En curso, Hecho). Checking off a step draws a marker check stroke, and a finished activity jumps to Hecho.\n\nDensity is calm and operational, built mobile first for a thumb. The board is the hero object: a framed white panel with a marker tray under it, holding the event title, the countdown, team progress, the dashed \"tu imán\" zone with your own markable steps, and the three-column mini board. Around it, plain white cards on aluminum hold the supporting lists. There is one sans (Figtree) and no gradients, glass or blur anywhere in the build. Depth comes from physical objects (the frame, magnets) rather than floating UI.\n\nThe world rejects the generic dashboard of white KPI cards with a progress ring over cream and terracotta.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Aluminum frame (#e8edf5) as the page, white enamel as every writing surface.",
      "Four markers with fixed jobs: blue acts, red warns and heads columns, green finishes, ink reads.",
      "People are magnets: colored dot plus name in a pill, with a short hard-edged drop shadow.",
      "Column-based progress (Pendiente / En curso / Hecho) instead of rings or KPI tiles.",
      "Marker-stroke check animation as the signature feedback.",
      "A single sans, Figtree, at heavy display weights (750 to 850) with tabular numerals."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Four Markers Rule",
        "body": "Blue acts, red warns or heads a column, green means done, ink reads. A marker never takes another marker's job. Blue is never a status, and green is never a call to action other than \"complete\".",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Contrast-Adapted Red Rule",
        "body": "Interface red is #d33a2c and its deep #b42d21. The brighter #E5483A belongs to the brand mark artwork only and never appears as text, border or fill in the UI.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Belongs-To-Me Rule",
        "body": "Anything that belongs to the current person (their magnet, task cards, roster row, member card) shifts to the blue wash or is outlined in Marker Blue Line. Nothing else uses that treatment.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Sans Rule",
        "body": "Figtree is the only family. Add emphasis with weight (650, 750, 800), never with a second face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Count Rule",
        "body": "Every number that counts days, steps, money or people uses tabular numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Real Magnet Rule",
        "body": "The magnet shadow is short and tight (2 to 3px) because a magnet sits flush on enamel. Never blur it into a floating glow, and never give it to things that are not movable markers of state or identity.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Frame Rule",
        "body": "Only the home board wears the aluminum frame and tray. Other surfaces are plain cards.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the page Aluminum Frame (#e8edf5) and every writing surface white enamel.",
      "Do use Marker Red #d33a2c (and #b42d21 for text on the red wash) for all interface red. Keep #E5483A inside the brand mark artwork only.",
      "Do represent people as magnets (colored dot plus name pill with the magnet shadow), and mark \"mine\" with the blue wash or a Marker Blue Line outline.",
      "Do show progress as columns (Pendiente / En curso / Hecho) with red uppercase column heads over a 2px blue rule, and as flat 8 to 12px progress tracks.",
      "Do give step completion the drawn green marker check (0.32s, out-expo).",
      "Do use tabular numerals for every count, date distance and amount.",
      "Do use dashed borders only to mean an open slot (\"tu imán\", empty columns, \"+N más\", the step editor)."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use gradients, glass or backdrop blur. The materials are enamel, aluminum and marker ink.",
      "Don't add a second typeface. Figtree carries every role.",
      "Don't build KPI tile rows or progress rings for the dashboard. The board and its columns are the progress display.",
      "Don't blur the magnet shadow into a soft floating glow, or put the aluminum frame and tray on anything but the home board.",
      "Don't use member or area data colors for UI chrome. They belong to dots, magnets and avatars.",
      "Don't use Marker Blue for status or Marker Green for anything but completion."
    ]
  }
